### Component Usage Rules

#### 0. Layout Components First (CONSISTENCY PRIORITY)
**ALWAYS check [components/layout/](mdc:apps/web/src/components/layout) FIRST before creating any UI elements**

- **Check existing layout components** before building new UI elements
- **Reuse layout patterns** from [headings.tsx](mdc:apps/web/src/components/layout/headings.tsx) and other layout files
- **Maintain visual consistency** by using established layout components
- **Extend layout components** rather than creating duplicates

**Layout Component Priority:**
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Check layout components first
import { H1, H2, Subtitle, DisplayHeading } from '@/components/layout/headings'
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'

function MyPage() {
  return (
    <div>
      <H1>Main Title</H1>      // Use existing heading styles
      <Subtitle>Supporting text</Subtitle>  // Use existing subtitle styles
      <Button>Action</Button>   // Then use shadcn/ui components
    </div>
  )
}

// ❌ WRONG: Creating custom headings when layout components exist
function MyPage() {
  return (
    <div>
      <h1 className="text-4xl font-bold">Title</h1>  // Don't recreate existing styles
      <p className="text-lg text-muted-foreground">Subtitle</p>  // Use layout components
    </div>
  )
}
```

**Layout Component Development Flow:**
1. **Check [components/layout/](mdc:apps/web/src/components/layout)** for existing components
2. **Use existing layout components** if they match your needs
3. **Extend layout components** if you need variations
4. **Create new layout components** only if truly unique
5. **Update layout components** if patterns should be reusable

#### 1. shadcn/ui Components (`components/ui/`)
- **Import and use directly** in your pages and components
- **Add shadcn components** using the CLI: `bunx shadcn@latest add button`
- **Customize with className** when needed using Tailwind utilities
- **No custom wrappers** - use the components as-is

**Usage Pattern:**
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Direct usage with Tailwind customization
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'
import { Card, CardContent, CardHeader, CardTitle } from '@/components/ui/card'

function MyComponent() {
  return (
    <Card className="bg-card/80 backdrop-blur-sm border-border/30">
      <CardHeader>
        <CardTitle className="text-foreground">My Title</CardTitle>
      </CardHeader>
      <CardContent>
        <Button 
          className="transition-all duration-200 hover:scale-105 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-purple-600"
          disabled={isLoading}
        >
          {isLoading ? "Loading..." : "Click me"}
        </Button>
      </CardContent>
    </Card>
  )
}

// ❌ WRONG: Creating custom wrapper components
function AppButton() { ... }  // Don't do this!
```

#### 2. Layout Components (`components/layout/`)
- **Only for layout-specific components** like headers, sidebars, page containers
- **Not shadcn-based components** - these are custom layout utilities
- **Keep minimal** - most components should be direct shadcn usage

## CSS Variable Usage Guidelines

### Priority Order for Styling
1. **CSS Variables (HIGHEST PRIORITY)**: Use existing CSS variables through Tailwind classes when available
2. **Tailwind Utilities**: Use standard Tailwind classes for additional styling
3. **Custom CSS**: Only for complex animations or unique requirements

### CSS Variables Available
From [globals.css](mdc:apps/web/src/app/globals.css):
```css
/* Colors - Use through Tailwind classes */
--color-background, --color-foreground, --color-primary, --color-muted, etc.
/* Example: bg-background, text-foreground, border-primary */

/* Fonts - Applied automatically via CSS variables */
--font-sans: Poppins, sans-serif  /* Default font family */
--font-serif: Poppins, sans-serif
--font-mono: Poppins, sans-serif
/* NO NEED for explicit font classes - Poppins is applied by default */

/* Shadows - Use through Tailwind classes */
--shadow-sm, --shadow-md, --shadow-lg, etc.
/* Example: shadow-sm, shadow-lg */

/* Custom animations */
--animate-dots: dots 1s infinite linear
/* Example: animate-dots for loading states */
```

**Examples:**
```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Using CSS variables through Tailwind
className="bg-background text-foreground border-primary shadow-lg"

// ✅ CORRECT: Font is automatically Poppins via CSS variables
className="font-medium"  // Uses Poppins automatically

// ❌ WRONG: Direct color values when CSS vars exist
className="bg-white text-black border-blue-500"

// ✅ CORRECT: Using available custom animation
className="animate-dots"

// ✅ CORRECT: Combining with Tailwind utilities
className="hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-200"
```

## Styling Guidelines

### Tailwind CSS v4 Configuration
- Use CSS-first configuration in [globals.css](mdc:apps/web/src/app/globals.css)
- Font: Poppins automatically applied via `--font-sans` CSS variable
- Leverage existing theme variables for consistent design
- Add custom animations using `@theme` directive with `@keyframes`

### Animation Principles
- **Subtle and Fast**: 200-300ms duration for most transitions
- **Purposeful**: Every animation should enhance understanding or feedback
- **Consistent Easing**: Use `ease-out`, `ease-in-out` for smooth feel
- **Hover States**: Gentle scale/shadow changes (`hover:scale-105`, `hover:shadow-lg`)
- **Focus States**: Clear focus indicators for accessibility
- **Loading States**: Use custom `animate-dots` for consistent loading indicators

### Common Styling Patterns
- **Glassmorphism**: `bg-background/80 backdrop-blur-sm border-border/30`
- **Hover Effects**: `hover:shadow-lg hover:-translate-y-0.5 active:scale-95`
- **Focus States**: `focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary`
- **Transitions**: `transition-all duration-200 ease-out`
- **Loading States**: `animate-dots` with three-dot animation

## Component Usage Examples

### Button Usage
```tsx
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'

// Default button
<Button>Click me</Button>

// Custom styled button
<Button className="bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-purple-600 hover:from-blue-600 hover:to-purple-700">
  Gradient Button
</Button>

// Loading state
<Button disabled={isLoading} className="transition-all duration-200">
  {isLoading ? (
    <div className="flex items-center gap-2">
      <div className="w-4 h-2 animate-dots bg-current opacity-60" />
      Loading...
    </div>
  ) : (
    "Submit"
  )}
</Button>
```

### Card Usage
```tsx
import { Card, CardContent, CardDescription, CardHeader, CardTitle } from '@/components/ui/card'

<Card className="bg-card/80 backdrop-blur-sm border-border/30 hover:bg-card/90 transition-all duration-200">
  <CardHeader>
    <CardTitle className="text-foreground">Card Title</CardTitle>
    <CardDescription className="text-muted-foreground">Card description</CardDescription>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent>
    <p>Card content goes here</p>
  </CardContent>
</Card>
```

### Form Usage
```tsx
import { Form, FormControl, FormField, FormItem, FormLabel, FormMessage } from '@/components/ui/form'
import { Input } from '@/components/ui/input'
import { Label } from '@/components/ui/label'

<Form {...form}>
  <form onSubmit={form.handleSubmit(onSubmit)} className="space-y-4">
    <FormField
      control={form.control}
      name="email"
      render={({ field }) => (
        <FormItem>
          <FormLabel className="font-medium text-foreground">Email</FormLabel>
          <FormControl>
            <Input 
              placeholder="Enter your email" 
              className="transition-all duration-200 focus-visible:shadow-lg"
              {...field} 
            />
          </FormControl>
          <FormMessage className="text-destructive" />
        </FormItem>
      )}
    />
  </form>
</Form>
```

## Development Best Practices

### 1. Component Import Strategy
```tsx
// Import what you need directly
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'
import { Card, CardContent, CardHeader, CardTitle } from '@/components/ui/card'
import { Input } from '@/components/ui/input'
import { Form, FormField, FormItem, FormLabel } from '@/components/ui/form'
```

### 2. Styling Approach
- **Use className prop** for all customizations
- **Leverage CSS variables** through Tailwind classes
- **Combine utilities** for complex effects
- **Maintain consistency** with app-wide design patterns

### 3. TypeScript Usage
- Import proper types from shadcn components
- Use `React.ComponentProps<typeof Component>` when extending
- Maintain type safety throughout the application

### 4. State Management
- Handle loading states in parent components
- Pass state through props to shadcn components
- Use proper disabled states and loading indicators

